  "principle": "POINTER-ONLY catalog of standard KNOWLEDGE / SUBJECT / NEWS classification systems (backs registry #81 knowledge_taxonomies) — how human information is organized: library classification (Dewey/LCC), knowledge graphs (Wikidata), domain taxonomies (MeSH medical, ACM computing, JEL economics, EuroVoc legal), news/media taxonomies (IPTC Media Topics + Event types), occupations (O*NET). Each entry says WHERE the scheme lives + its scope + machine-readability, NEVER a copy of the taxonomy data. serves_truth=false. The 'what is this ABOUT' map the compiler uses to route + classify subject matter (distinct from #20 semantic_ontology, which aliases FIELD NAMES).",
  "serves_truth": false,
